{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBoundedJucysMurphy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBoundedJucysMurphy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBoundedGenerators"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_jmRaw_one_of_below","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_jmRaw_one_of_below","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJucysMurphy.lean#L141-L145","doc":"Recovers `sigma_comm_jmRaw_one` from the bounded form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_jmRawB_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_jmRawB_one","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJucysMurphy.lean#L130-L139","doc":"`σⱼ` commutes with `L₂ = σ₀²` whenever `j ≥ 2` and `σⱼ` is a generator of `H_n(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_prod_three_of_below","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_prod_three_of_below","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJucysMurphy.lean#L122-L126","doc":"Recovers `jmRaw_prod_three` from the bounded form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRawB_prod_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRawB_prod_three","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJucysMurphy.lean#L109-L120","doc":"**`∏Lᵢ = Δ²` at `n = 3`.**  One application of the braid relation to the middle three letters.\n\nOnly `braid 0` is used, so the hypothesis is `2 < n` — exactly \"`σ₀` and `σ₁` are both generators\nof `H_n(q)`\".  The Hecke relation is not needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRawB_prod_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRawB_prod_two","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJucysMurphy.lean#L103-L107","doc":"**`∏Lᵢ = Δ²` at `n = 2`** — immediate from the recursion, no relation used at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.fullTwist3B","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.fullTwist3B","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJucysMurphy.lean#L100-L101","doc":"The full twist of `B₃`: `Δ² = (σ₀σ₁)³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.fullTwist2B","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.fullTwist2B","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJucysMurphy.lean#L97-L98","doc":"The full twist of `B₂`: `Δ² = σ₀²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_closed_two_of_below","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_closed_two_of_below","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJucysMurphy.lean#L89-L93","doc":"Recovers `jmRaw_closed_two` from the bounded form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRawB_closed_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRawB_closed_two","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJucysMurphy.lean#L84-L87","doc":"**`L₂ = (q − q⁻¹)σ₀ + 1`.**  Needs `σ₀` to be a generator of `H_n(q)`, i.e. `1 < n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmB_toBelow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmB_toBelow","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJucysMurphy.lean#L77-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmB_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmB_succ","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJucysMurphy.lean#L74-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmB_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmB_zero","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJucysMurphy.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmB","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJucysMurphy.lean#L67-L70","doc":"**`q`-normalized JM elements** on the bounded presentation: `L_{i+1} = q⁻¹ σᵢ Lᵢ σᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRawB_toBelow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRawB_toBelow","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJucysMurphy.lean#L59-L63","doc":"The JM elements of the downcast are the original JM elements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.toBelow_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.toBelow_σ","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJucysMurphy.lean#L56-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGenerators.toBelow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGenerators.toBelow","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJucysMurphy.lean#L47-L54","doc":"**Downcast.**  `H_∞(q)`'s relations hold at every index, so in particular at every index below\n`n`.  This is what makes the bounded class a generalization rather than a parallel development. ","signatureChunk":0}]}